/*
Every expression of four and/or operators on five boolean variables, every
way of grouping them (fully in parentheses), each as a value and as an if
condition, for all 32 combinations of true and false (a, b, c, d, e: FFFFF, ...,
TTTTT). Each line shows the 32 values and the 32 choices the if made, as T or F.
The variables keep the compiler from working the answer out in advance, as
it can with the literal true and false of Expressions/BoolParens.

Deeper groupings, so a fix to how and/or jump at runtime is checked well
beyond the shape where the bug was found.
*/
class Main
